  "goal": "Shop, ask prices, haggle and count your change — in the busiest and most enjoyable place to practice Hebrew.",
  "bekal": [
    "asking about prices and quantities",
    "asking for amounts and naming units",
    "haggling and paying politely"
  ],
  "dialogs": [
    {
      "title": "שִׂיחָה — שׁוּק הַכַּרְמֶל",
      "intro": "Budi is shopping at the Carmel Market in Tel Aviv. The vendor, Moshe, is shouting out his goods.",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "מֹשֶׁה:",
          "text": "עַגְבָנִיּוֹת! חָמֵשׁ שֶׁקֶל לְקִילוֹ!",
          "baca": "agvaniyot! khamesh shekel lekilo!",
          "id": "Tomatoes! Five shekels a kilo!",
          "literal": "tomatoes! five shekel for-kilo!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "סְלִיחָה, כַּמָּה עוֹלוֹת הַתַּפּוּזִים?",
          "baca": "slikhah, kamah olot hatapuzim?",
          "id": "Excuse me, how much are the oranges?",
          "literal": "sorry, how-much rise (pl f) the-oranges?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "מֹשֶׁה:",
          "text": "שְׁמוֹנָה שֶׁקֶל לְקִילוֹ. הֵם מְתוּקִים!",
          "baca": "shmonah shekel lekilo. hem metukim!",
          "id": "Eight shekels a kilo. They're sweet!",
          "literal": "eight shekel for-kilo. they sweet (pl)!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "אֶפְשָׁר שְׁנֵי קִילוֹ, בְּבַקָּשָׁה?",
          "baca": "efshar shnei kilo, bevakashah?",
          "id": "Could I have two kilos, please?",
          "literal": "possible two kilo, with-request?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "מֹשֶׁה:",
          "text": "בְּוַדַּאי. עוֹד מַשֶּׁהוּ?",
          "baca": "bevadai. od mashehu?",
          "id": "Of course. Anything else?",
          "literal": "with-certainty. more something?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "חֲצִי קִילוֹ עַגְבָנִיּוֹת וּשְׁלוֹשָׁה מְלָפְפוֹנִים.",
          "baca": "khatsi kilo agvaniyot ushloshah melafefonim.",
          "id": "Half a kilo of tomatoes and three cucumbers.",
          "literal": "half kilo tomatoes and-three cucumbers."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "מֹשֶׁה:",
          "text": "הַכֹּל בְּיַחַד עֶשְׂרִים וְאַרְבָּעָה שֶׁקֶל.",
          "baca": "hakol beyakhad esrim ve'arba'ah shekel.",
          "id": "That's twenty-four shekels altogether.",
          "literal": "the-all together twenty and-four shekel."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "זֶה קְצָת יָקָר, לֹא?",
          "baca": "zeh ktsat yakar, lo?",
          "id": "That's a bit expensive, isn't it?",
          "literal": "this a-little expensive, no?"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "מֹשֶׁה:",
          "text": "טוֹב, עֶשְׂרִים. רַק בִּשְׁבִילְךָ.",
          "baca": "tov, esrim. rak bishvilkha.",
          "id": "OK, twenty. Just for you.",
          "literal": "good, twenty. only for-you."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "תּוֹדָה! הִנֵּה חֲמִשִּׁים.",
          "baca": "todah! hineh khamishim.",
          "id": "Thanks! Here's fifty.",
          "literal": "thanks! here fifty."
        },
        {
          "speaker": "מֹשֶׁה:",
          "text": "וְהָעֹדֶף — שְׁלוֹשִׁים שֶׁקֶל. בְּתֵאָבוֹן!",
          "baca": "veha'odef — shloshim shekel. bete'avon!",
          "id": "And your change — thirty shekels. Enjoy!",
          "literal": "and-the-change — thirty shekel. with-appetite!"
        },
        {
          "speaker": "בּוּדִי:",
          "text": "תּוֹדָה רַבָּה. יוֹם טוֹב!",
          "baca": "todah rabah. yom tov!",
          "id": "Thanks a lot. Have a good day!",
          "literal": "thanks much. day good!"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        "**כַּמָּה עוֹלֶה?** (\"how much does it cost?\") changes form to match the item, because עוֹלֶה is a verb. One masculine item: כַּמָּה עוֹלֶה הַסֵּפֶר? One feminine item: כַּמָּה עוֹלָה הַמַּחְבֶּרֶת? Plural: כַּמָּה עוֹלִים / עוֹלוֹת. If you don't know what the item is, use the default form: **כַּמָּה זֶה עוֹלֶה?**",
        "⚠️ **Price units use לְ־.** חָמֵשׁ שֶׁקֶל לְקִילוֹ = \"five shekels per kilo\". Exactly the same pattern as לְחֹדֶשׁ (per month) and לְשִׁעוּר (per lesson), which you've already seen.",
        "**שֶׁקֶל isn't made plural when quoting prices.** People say עֶשְׂרִים שֶׁקֶל, not עֶשְׂרִים שְׁקָלִים — even though the plural exists and is used in formal contexts. Market habit beats grammar here.",
        "**Fruit and vegetable names are almost always feminine plural (־וֹת) or masculine plural (־ִים)** because you buy them in quantity: עַגְבָנִיּוֹת (tomatoes), מְלָפְפוֹנִים (cucumbers), תַּפּוּזִים (oranges). The singular is rare unless you really are buying just one.",
        "**בִּשְׁבִיל** (*bishvil*, \"for\") also takes endings: בִּשְׁבִילִי (for me), בִּשְׁבִילְךָ (for you). The same ending machine again — the third time you've seen it, after שֶׁל and אֶת.",
        "**Haggling in Israel has its limits.** In a שׁוּק (open-air market) haggling is normal, especially just before Shabbat when vendors want to clear their stock. In shops, supermarkets and restaurants you **don't** haggle at all. A gentle way to open: זֶה קְצָת יָקָר, לֹא? — exactly what Budi says.",
        "**עֹדֶף** (*odef*) = change. If you want to pay exact, the full sentence is: אֵין לִי עֹדֶף (I don't have small change).",
        "**הִנֵּה** (*hineh*) = \"here you go, here it is\". Used when handing something over. Very common, and it never changes form."
      ],
