          "type": "p",
          "text": "⚠️ **תַּפּוּחַ אֲדָמָה** literally means \"earth apple\" — that's a potato. Modern Hebrew often strings two old words together for a new thing: תַּפּוּז (orange) itself is a blend of תַּפּוּחַ + זָהָב, \"golden apple\"."
        },
        {
          "type": "p",
          "text": "Israel's busiest markets: **שׁוּק הַכַּרְמֶל** in Tel Aviv, **מַחֲנֵה יְהוּדָה** in Jerusalem, and **שׁוּק הָעִיר הָעַתִּיקָה** in Akko. All of them are far busier — and far cheaper — **on Friday morning**."
